From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:25:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: afk: Fail when the endpoint does not start

Return the RTKit error instead of sending the init message to an
endpoint that was never started and timing out a second later.

[Youwes09: from Gravity Linux 83fb190f1108]
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c
index c861cf07cff4..7f9c4beca45d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c
@@ -162,7 +162,9 @@ int afk_start(struct apple_dcp_afkep *ep)
 	int ret;
 
 	reinit_completion(&ep->started);
-	apple_rtkit_start_ep(ep->dcp->rtk, ep->endpoint);
+	ret = apple_rtkit_start_ep(ep->dcp->rtk, ep->endpoint);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 	afk_send(ep, FIELD_PREP(RBEP_TYPE, RBEP_INIT));
 
 	ret = wait_for_completion_timeout(&ep->started, msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
